📘 Repository Description (for GitHub short summary box)

Data-driven analysis of YouTube statistics across the globe using Excel. This project explores global trends in YouTube content performance, including views, likes, comments, engagement rates, and regional insights — visualized through data cleaning, analysis, and dashboards.

🧠 README (Detailed Project Description)
📊 Project Overview

The Global YouTube Statistics Analysis project explores worldwide YouTube data to uncover insights into viewer engagement, video performance, and creator reach. Using the dataset in Global YouTube Statistics.xlsx, the project aims to identify top-performing regions, content types, and engagement metrics that drive success on YouTube.

🎯 Objectives

Analyze and interpret key YouTube metrics (views, likes, comments, and subscribers).

Identify the countries and creators with the highest engagement rates.

Discover patterns and correlations between video performance and audience behavior.

Visualize global YouTube trends using charts and dashboards.

⚙️ Tools & Technologies Used
Tool / Language	Purpose
Microsoft Excel	Data cleaning, pivot tables, charting
Power Query	Data transformation and filtering
Power BI / Tableau (optional)	Advanced visual analytics
Python (Pandas, Matplotlib, Seaborn)	Optional statistical analysis
GitHub	Version control and sharing of analysis
🧩 Dataset Description

The Excel file Global YouTube Statistics.xlsx contains structured data on:

Country — origin of the YouTube channel or audience

Channel Name — unique name of each creator

Subscribers — total number of subscribers

Views — cumulative video views

Uploads — number of uploaded videos

Engagement Metrics — likes, comments, shares, etc.

📈 Key Insights (Example Outcomes)

Top 10 countries with the highest YouTube engagement.

Correlation between upload frequency and total subscribers.

Comparative visualization of average views per country.

Identification of emerging creator regions.

🧰 Features

Cleaned and structured Excel dataset for further analysis.

Interactive dashboards and charts visualizing YouTube trends.

Easy-to-use dataset for academic, research, or business projects.

🏆 Future Improvements

Add automated Python scripts for data cleaning.

Integrate Power BI dashboards for interactive exploration.

Include predictive analytics using machine learning models.
